    "All figures transcribed from the nutrition panels on starbucks.com product pages (www.starbucks.com/menu/product/<id>/<hot|iced|single>/nutrition), 2026-10-05. Drinks are Grande (16 fl oz) with the standard recipe and default milk (2% for lattes/mochas; coconutmilk for Pink Drink and Dragon Drink; oatmilk for the Brown Sugar Shaken Espresso); Espresso is listed Solo and Doppio; Cortado is Short only. Food is one serving as sold.",
    "Starbucks does not publish per-pump syrup or per-splash milk nutrition on starbucks.com (the site recalculates customized drinks as a whole), so no per-unit syrup or alternative-milk components are included. The latte milk, sweet-cream, cold-foam and sauce components here are derived by subtracting one published grande drink from another (see each component's \"derived\"); builds are only given where that subtraction is clean (lattes, mochas, PSL, cold brews, Americano).",
    "Omitted: Trenta/Venti sizes, seasonal and limited items beyond Pumpkin Spice Latte and Pumpkin Cream Cold Brew, protein beverages, energy refreshers, bottled drinks, packaged snacks, lunch boxes."
